// @check
// @error __array_new_default__ fills every slot with the element's default value, and string has none — use __array_new__(n, fill)
// CONTRACT (must-error): `array.new_default` writes each slot's ZERO, and a `string` element
// has none — VL's string is non-nullable and `let s: string` with no initialiser is a
// definite-assignment error, not `""`. The same holds for a struct, a closure, a map, a nested
// list, a union and anything nullable: the instruction would write a WasmGC null, or a niche
// sentinel that is not a member of its own type.
//
// It is a DESIGN rule, so it is a plain type error and not an `unsupported-lowering`
// concession — `__array_new__(n, fill)` is the spelling that serves these elements. And it is
// raised in the CHECKER: reaching the emitter with this meant building the i32 backing under a
// `string[]` destination, which was `vl check` rc 0 and invalid wasm. D1470.
const zs: string[] = __array_new_default__(6)
print(zs.length)
